## Scope

Build an experimental Zotero 10 extension that warms native SDT packs through
`Zotero.SDT.ensure`, with a toolbar status dialog and no private durable ledger.
The author wants a launchable build tonight. It does not patch Zotero's worker,
replace source PDFs, or change native flat-text indexing preferences.

Use the previously tested native contract and passive pack inspection from
`verification/SDT-DIAGNOSTIC-LIVE.md` and
`verification/SDT-PLUGIN-PREREQUISITES.md`. Graceful disable is owned by
SPEC.md R22. Resource policy awaits the author's confirmation in this session.

## Acceptance

- One outstanding admission, non-priority native ensure, yield between items.
- Reconstruct coverage from native cache metadata; suppress failures for the
  session, without retrying unresolved native work.
- Disable removes timers/UI and prevents further admissions; submitted work
  may finish without updating detached UI.
- Explicitly disclose shared-worker non-preemption and absent OS nice control.
- Show coverage, failures, active item, native progress, last progress age,
  empirical speed/ETA and native full-text statistics.
- Unit tests and isolated real-Zotero smoke test before providing the XPI.
- No automatic installation into the author's live profile by the test harness.

## Delivery evidence

`verification/SDT-SITTER-LAUNCH.md` documents installation, limits and reproduction.
`bench/results/sdt-sitter-launch-2026-09-05/integration.json` records the passing
isolated native application run and exact source digests. The extension is in
`bench/sdt-sitter/`, the packager in `bench/build_sdt_sitter.py`, and deterministic
scheduler/estimator tests in `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs`.
